{title: Home on the Range}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}
{capo: 2}

{start_of_tab: Intro}
e|-----------------|
B|-----------------|
G|---0-------0-----|
D|-----------------|
A|-----------------|
E|-3-------3-------|
{end_of_tab}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Oh, give me a [C]home where the [G]buffalo roam,
Where the [G]deer and the [D7]antelope [G]play;
Where [G]seldom is [C]heard a dis[G]couraging word,
And the [Am]skies are not [D7]cloudy all [G]day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Home, home on the [C]range,
Where the [G]deer and the [D7]antelope [G]play;
Where [G]seldom is [C]heard a dis[G]couraging word,
And the [Am]skies are not [D7]cloudy all [G]day.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
How [G]often at night when the [C]heavens are [G]bright
With the [G]light from the [D7]glittering [G]stars,
Have I [G]stood here a[C]mazed and asked [G]as I gazed
If their [Am]glory ex[D7]ceeds that of [G]ours.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
